[al:新概念英语第三册]
[ti:13. It’s Only Me]
[00:00.840]Passage 13. | 第13篇。
[00:02.585]It's only me. | 只是我。
[00:05.105]After her husband had gone to work, | 她丈夫去上班后，
[00:08.195]Mrs. Richards sent her children to school and went upstairs to her bedroom. | 理查兹夫人送孩子们上学，然后上楼回到自己的卧室。
[00:12.735]She was too excited to do any housework that morning. | 她那天早上太兴奋了，什么家务也做不了。
[00:15.930]For in the evening, she would be going to a fancy dress party with her husband. | 因为那天晚上，她要和丈夫一起去参加一个化装舞会。
[00:20.955]She intended to dress up as a ghost, | 她打算打扮成一个鬼魂，
[00:23.815]and as she had made her costume the night before, she was impatient to try it on. | 既然前一晚她已经做好了戏服，她就迫不及待地想试穿。
[00:28.820]Though the costume consisted only of a sheet, it was very effective. | 尽管这套戏服只是一块床单，但效果非常好。
[00:33.300]After putting it on, Mrs. Richards went downstairs. | 穿上之后，理查兹夫人下了楼。
[00:37.205]She wanted to find out whether it would be comfortable to wear. | 她想看看穿起来是否舒服。
[00:40.950]Just as Mrs. Richards was entering the dining room, there was a knock on the front door. | 就在理查兹夫人走进餐厅的时候，前门传来一阵敲门声。
[00:46.200]She knew that it must be the baker. | 她知道那一定是面包师。
[00:48.245]She had told him to come straight in if ever she failed to open the door and to leave the bread on the kitchen table. | 她曾告诉过他，如果她没有开门，就直接进来，把面包留在厨房的桌子上。
[00:54.735]Not wanting to frighten the poor man, | 不想吓到那个可怜的人，
[00:57.335]Mrs. Richards quickly hid in the small storeroom under the stairs. | 理查兹夫人迅速躲到了楼梯下的小储藏室里。
[01:01.420]She heard the front door open and heavy footsteps in the hall. | 她听到前门开了，大厅里传来沉重的脚步声。
[01:05.940]Suddenly, the door of the storeroom was opened and a man entered. | 突然，储藏室的门开了，一个人走了进来。
[01:10.280]Mrs. Richards realized that it must be the man from the electricity board who had come to read the meter. | 理查兹夫人意识到，那一定是电力公司的抄表员。
[01:16.035]She tried to explain the situation saying, | 她试图解释情况，说：
[01:18.870]"It's only me!" But it was too late. | “只是我！”但为时已晚。
[01:22.005]The man let out a cry and jumped back several paces. | 那人发出一声尖叫，后退了好几步。
[01:25.965]When Mrs. Richards walked towards him, he fled, | 当理查兹夫人走向他时，他逃走了，
[01:29.195]slamming the door behind him. | 砰地一声关上了身后的门。